      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "It appears that this previously fixed Cloth scaling issue has regressed in the current version of VRChat.\n\nThis report was marked as **Complete on April 22, 2024**, but the same issue is occurring again.\n\n**Reproduction steps:**\n\n1. Wear an avatar that uses the Unity Cloth component.\n\n2. Change the avatar's height using VRChat's built-in Avatar Height adjustment.\n\n3. The avatar's body scales correctly, but the Cloth mesh does not scale properly with it.\n\nThis issue was previously addressed in VRChat 2023.3.2 and 2023.4.2.\n\nDuring the Unity 2022 migration, a developer explained in this thread that changes to Unity's internal Cloth simulation caused the previous Unity 2019 fix to stop working.\n\nSince VRChat has recently migrated to Unity 6, I am concerned that a similar regression may have occurred again.\n\nThere is also another potentially related issue where Cloth scaling is affected by the height of the previously used avatar:\n\nhttps://feedback.vrchat.com/bug-reports/p/1920-cloth-scale-changes-on-last-avatar-height\n\nBoth issues may be related to how Cloth scaling is initialized or updated, although the underlying cause is not yet known.\n\nThe current tracked report for the avatar height adjustment issue is here:\n\nhttps://feedback.vrchat.com/bug-reports/p/cloth-applied-mesh-does-not-scale-when-avatar-scale-is-changed\n\nCould you please investigate whether the previous Cloth scaling fix has regressed, and consider reopening this report?",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-08-30T01:21:56.004Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Thank you for responding to the cloth scaling issue in the Unity2019 open beta the other day.\n\nWhen I conducted a similar test today at the open beta for Unity 2022,\n\nThe incident has recurred, so please take action.\n\nUnlike the previous bug, this recurring issue does not reflect the changed scale even if the Cloth component is reset by turning it on and off, making it impossible for the user to take temporary measures. I'm here.",
